The exported cabi_realloc is internal/wasi's //go:wasmexport, a bump allocator that allocates nothing from the
Go heap, not the trap stand-in that p3exit0 and p3panic export.

F1's two components were rebuilt from their committed sources on this toolchain. They are not byte-identical,
and every differing byte is the toolchain's identity: the Go build ID's hashes and the go1.28-devel version
string. Rebuilt once more with a VERSION file forcing F1's version string, only the build ID's first 20 bytes
differ (17 for p3panic), and those hash the toolchain's own binaries. The code and every other section are
unchanged, because a program that links no bindings gets the linker's stand-in exactly as before.
